Okay, let's evaluate the 'Mercedes-Benz CLS CLS350 CDI V6'.

As explained previously, the designation "CLS 350 CDI" (which used a V6 engine) belongs to the older generations of the CLS (C219 and C218). The *most recent* generation (C257, 2018-present) does not use this specific designation or a V6 diesel engine.

The modern equivalent in the current lineup, representing the higher-performance six-cylinder diesel, is the **Mercedes-Benz CLS 400d**. This model uses a 3.0L *inline*-six turbo-diesel engine.

Therefore, I will evaluate the **Mercedes-Benz CLS 400d (C257)** as the most relevant modern counterpart to the older CLS 350 CDI V6.

